** TODO The integer limit strings of =22.locale.num.get= keep arms for a 16-bit =long=

=test_long= and =test_ulong= in
=tests/localization/22.locale.num.get.cpp= pick their limit strings
by ~LONG_MAX == 0x7fffL~ and ~ULONG_MAX == 0xffffUL~ first, and
=test_pvoid= by ~ULONG_MAX == 0xffffUL~. ISO C gives =LONG_MAX= a
minimum of 2147483647, so no implementation takes those arms.

Fix: the three arms leave; each chain starts at the 32-bit arm.

Check: =22.locale.num.get= in 15D is at its pin on an LP64 host.

** TODO The =--enable-num_get= mode of =22.locale.num.put= fails 552 assertions

=tests/localization/22.locale.num.put.cpp= reads each row's output
back through =num_get= under =--enable-num_get=. Off by default, so no
pin sees it. In 15D under GCC it fails 552 of 4115 assertions: 6 per
row of =inf_nan_test= (lines 1365-1473 after the =ullong_test= rows),
where =num_get= stores 0 with =failbit= for "inf", "INF" and "-inf",
and 2 per row at 1635-1638, 1722-1724 and 1734-1738 of the
floating tests. The atoms of stage 2, 14882:2003 22.2.2.1.2 p8, hold
no "i" or "n", so the infinity rows may be expectations the mode
should skip, as it skips a negative precision. Seen while adding the
=ullong_test= rows, 2026-11-21; those rows round-trip clean.

Fix: skip the rows whose output =num_get= is not required to read,
or record why each fails.

Check: =22.locale.num.put --enable-num_get= in 15D: 0 failed, or each
failure explained.

** TODO =rw_any_t= takes a =signed char= or =unsigned char= pointer as =const void*=

=tests/include/rw_any.h= declares constructors for =char= and
=wchar_t= pointers but none for =signed char*= or =unsigned char*=, so
such a pointer converts to =const void*=. =type_name= then reads
"const void*" and =tostr= formats the address with =%p=. The rows of
=27.ostream='s =test_formatted= that insert ~(const signed char*)~ and
~(const unsigned char*)~ strings thus name their type "const void*"
and, when they fail, print an address for the value: a scratch row
that inserts "A" and expects "a" reports ~operator<<(const void* =
00005563be1b6d70) inserted "A", expected "a"~. Seen while making the
failed output row of =27.ostream= print its value, 2026-11-21.

Fix: =rw_any_t= takes the =signed char= and =unsigned char= pointers
(the four cv forms of each, as for =char=), with their type ids and
names, and =tostr= formats them as strings.

Check: the scratch row prints ~(const signed char* = A)~; the tests
that include =rw_any.h= hold at pin.

