** TODO =UserClass='s destructor throws, and the dialect makes it =noexcept=

=UserClass::~UserClass= (=tests/src/value.cpp= 143) throws =Dtor=
when =dtor_throw_ptr_= points at the count of destructor calls so far.
GCC's default dialect is C++17, where a destructor without an
exception specification is =noexcept=, so the throw calls
=std::terminate=; GCC 16 says so with =-Wterminate= at line 157. No
test sets =dtor_throw_ptr_= or the =dtor_throw_count_= it points at
by default (=git grep dtor_throw tests= finds the declarations in
=tests/include/rw_value.h= and the uses in =value.cpp= only), so the
throw is never reached in the suite. Seen
while rebuilding the driver, 2026-11-21.

Fix: a decision. Either the destructor takes =noexcept (false)= where
the dialect has it, gated by a characterization as the tree gates any
dialect feature, or the knob, its =dtor_throw_count_= default and its
=Dtor= exception leave as an interface no test uses. Read the history
of =dtor_throw_ptr_= first.

Check: =rwtest= builds without the =-Wterminate= warning; the
container tests that use =UserClass= hold at pin.

** TODO =23.vector.allocator= draws =-Wdeprecated-copy= from the headers

