=23.vector.allocator=: the implicit copy assignment of
=Pointer<MyClass>= is deprecated, since =Pointer= (59) has a
user-provided copy constructor (72) and no copy assignment. The
warnings name the library's headers, and their notes name the test.
Seen while the warnings of the container tests were cleared,
2026-11-21.

Fix: =Pointer= declares its copy assignment, or loses the copy
constructor, which copies =offset_= as the implicit one would.

Check: =23.vector.allocator= builds in 15D with no
=-Wdeprecated-copy=; its row at pin.

** TODO The archetypes of the numeric tests draw =-Wdeprecated-copy=

GCC 16 in 15D warns =-Wdeprecated-copy= on =26.accumulate= and
=26.inner.product=: =Accumulator= (and =Multiplicator=) declare a
private copy assignment to be not assignable, so their implicit copy
constructor is deprecated, and the algorithm copies them (16 and 16
warnings at the call of 26.inner.product 202, 4 at 26.accumulate
175); =Y= has a user-provided copy constructor, so its implicit copy
assignment, which =include/numeric= 59 and 69 apply, is deprecated (8
warnings); =plus_op<assign<base<cpy_ctor> > >= of each test draws two
more through =rw_alg_test.h=. The archetypes are meant to be copyable
and not assignable. Hypothesis: =26.partial.sum= and
=26.adjacent.diff=, whose =Accumulator= has the same shape, and the
other users of =rw_alg_test.h='s =base= draw the same; only the two
tests above were built and read. Seen while the call counts of the
two tests were read, 2026-11-21.

Fix: each archetype declares the copy constructor it relies on, so the
implicit one is not used; =base= of =rw_alg_test.h= the same.

Check: the =numerics= tests build in 15D with no =-Wdeprecated-copy=;
their rows at pin.

